          explanation: 'Both fences have to be worked out and both have to be tested, even when the answer looks obvious from the list. The 1.5 × IQR rule is a convention, not a law of nature: it marks values far enough from the middle half to be worth a second look. Finding an outlier is not a reason to delete it — it is a reason to ask whether it is a mistake in the recording or a real and interesting value.',
