          answer: 'f(x) > g(x) means x² − 4 > 3x, so x² − 3x − 4 > 0, which factorises as (x − 4)(x + 1) > 0. A product of two factors is positive when both are positive or both are negative. Both are positive when x > 4; both are negative when x < −1. So f(x) > g(x) for x < −1 or x > 4. Between −1 and 4 the parabola lies BELOW the line, and at x = −1 and x = 4 the graphs meet.',
